  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 121 PM MDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nMain impact today remains heat advisory in effect until 8 pm for\nmuch of southeast Idaho. Temperatures will reach 100 in many\nlocations late this afternoon. Expect isolated thunderstorms\nmainly over the southern hills once again this afternoon and do\nexpect nocturnal showers overnight again mainly in high\nelevations. It will remain hot Tuesday but will cool a couple of\ndegrees and convective activity will be more widespread. By\nWednesday an embedded short wave moving through Idaho should\nenhance significantly the shower and thunderstorm coverage with\nsignificantly cooler temperatures with many low elevation highs\ndown to the upper 80s. Expecting much drier conditions Thursday\nthrough next Monday with only isolated mountain storms expected.\nHot temperatures return with low elevations mainly in the 90s\nFriday through Monday and mountains in the 80s.",
